WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.490
Ever since Avengers: Infinity War ended, fans
have been speculating over just who is going

00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.560
to actually be in 2019's Avengers 4.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.580
Rumors are swirling that the film will feature
pretty much every character in the entire

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:16.070
Marvel Cinematic Universe, with stars revealing
they filmed one scene that included nearly

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.640
three dozen heroes.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.840
"I think in one particular scene there's like
32..

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.000
There's a lot of us There's so many of us!"

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.920
But it turns out some of your favorites still
won't join the party.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:26.760
Why?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.120
Here's a look at some Marvel characters who
will not be in Avengers 4.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:31.780
Adam Warlock

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:37.300
Avengers 4 co-director Joe Russo dashed the
hopes of some fans when he made it clear Adam

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.900
Warlock would not be appearing in Avengers
4.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.899
Warlock was a pivotal figure in the 1991 comic
book miniseries Infinity Gauntlet from which

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:47.560
Avengers: Infinity War takes much of its inspiration.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:52.820
One of Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2's mid-credits
scenes fed fans' expectations that Warlock

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:55.280
would appear in either Infinity War or its
sequel.

00:00:56.440 --> 00:00:57.740
"I think I shall call him…

00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:01.240
Adam"

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:04.820
Regardless, Russo told ComicBook.com it isn't
happening.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:09.000
"I have no interest as a director in telling
a story that's already been told or in seeing

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.200
one that's already been told.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.330
If I know all the events […] as they're
going to happen, then what's the point of

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:14.140
going to the film?"

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:18.820
Plus, with director James Gunn no longer running
the Guardians of the Galaxy franchise, there's

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.620
no telling now whether Warlock will ever show
up at all.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:22.540
Bummer.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.880
The X-Men and the Fantastic Four

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.980
In spite of rumors to the contrary, Marvel
Studios president Kevin Feige insists that

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:34.900
neither the X-Men nor the Fantastic Four will
appear in Avengers 4 even if Disney's planned

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:39.500
acquisition of Fox goes through as planned,
partly because Avengers 4 has already been

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.540
filmed, and the editing process has already
begun.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:46.030
Feige told the Daily News that when it comes
to the X-Men and the Fantastic Four potentially

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:47.229
joining the MCU,

00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:49.320
"I have vague dreams and vague ideas.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:53.820
But right now, bringing to life the 10,000-plus
characters that Marvel fully controls is what

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:54.560
the gameplan is."

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.160
Marvel's Netflix heroes

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.260
If you're hoping to see the cast of Netflix's
Defenders or Punisher in Avengers 4, you should

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:04.720
probably go ahead and feel the disappointment
now.

00:02:05.369 --> 00:02:10.440
In March 2018, Joe Russo told Premiere the
Netflix heroes were considered for inclusion

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.779
in Avengers: Infinity War, but it would've
been too much to juggle, especially with so

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.450
many different directors involved.

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:20.439
"[T]he trick is that we already have at least
sixty characters with whom we must tell a

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:20.940
story!

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:25.739
And it's hard enough to communicate with Taika
Waititi, Ryan Coogler, Scott Derrickson, Peyton

00:02:25.739 --> 00:02:30.689
Reed and James Gunn at the same time, not
to add all the showrunners and TV crews to

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:32.680
this … So it's practically impossible.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:37.020
Our job is to focus on the Marvel film world
and offer a satisfying climax."'

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.580
Of course, in the interview Russo was talking
specifically about Infinity War, not Avengers

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.720
4, but it's safe to assume it applies to Avengers
4 as well.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.760
"Oh my god, this is the dumbest"

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.480
Silver Surfer

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.480
Before the release of Avengers: Infinity War,
rumors flew around the web that Silver Surfer

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.300
would make a surprise appearance in the film.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.780
Spoilers: he didn't.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:02.689
And while the rumor mill is just getting started
when it comes to Avengers 4, you probably

00:03:02.689 --> 00:03:06.600
shouldn't believe any reports you hear about
Silver Surfer making a cameo in it.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.680
Like the X-Men and the Fantastic Four, the
rights to Silver Surfer are held up in the

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.180
Disney-Fox acquisition.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:16.819
Even if that gets resolved before Avengers
4 comes out, expect Silver Surfer to make

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.560
his debut later rather than sooner.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.340
Deadpool

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:25.180
As soon as Disney's attempt to acquire Fox
was announced, Deadpool star Ryan Reynolds

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:29.320
trolled the Mouse House by re-tweeting a picture
of Deadpool being escorted out of Disneyland.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:34.440
Later, after the success of Avengers: Infinity
War, Reynolds tweeted congratulations to the

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:38.320
team by posting what he said was his Avengers
rejection letter from Tony Stark.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.440
Hey, given what happened to his last team,
can you really blame them?

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.799
"but there is a slight chance that Vanisher
could make it…

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.120
Nope... no chance, he's dead."

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:52.290
But while fans have pushed all sorts of theories
about how and why Deadpool may make a surprise

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.939
appearance in Avengers 4, it seems very unlikely
given Deadpool faces the same rights challenges

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.600
as the X-Men, Fantastic Four, and Silver Surfer.

00:04:01.209 --> 00:04:05.100
For the time being, he'll just have to do
as the Avengers rejection letter suggested

00:04:05.109 --> 00:04:06.859
and stick with bothering Professor X.

00:04:06.859 --> 00:04:08.900
"how about those pots with the giant pigeon
wings?

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.180
What do those do anyway?

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:13.480
Carry him three feet off the ground to pick
up the nearest muffin crumb?"

